{"metadata":{"title":"TrackerTesting","modules":[{"name":"TrackerTesting"}],"symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"TrackerTesting","role":"collection"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/trackertesting"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Recording a body’s events","anchor":"Recording-a-bodys-events","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting\/withRecordingTracker(_:)-8blfh","doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting\/withRecordingTracker(_:)-mlec","doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting\/withRecordingTracker(_:)-26pul","doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting\/withRecordingTracker(_:)-pnmv"]},{"title":"Reading what was tracked","anchor":"Reading-what-was-tracked","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting\/TrackerRecording"]}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Run a test’s body with a fresh tracker and check the events it tracked, in order."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"withRecordingTracker","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" makes a tracker, binds it to the current task with "},{"code":"withTracker","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"length of its body, then finishes it and returns a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting\/TrackerRecording"},{"type":"text","text":" of every event tracked"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through it. Each call makes its own tracker, so tests that run at once never see each other’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events. Events tracked after the body returns, by work it started but didn’t wait for, are dropped."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"There are four spellings. The body can be synchronous or asynchronous, and it can take the tracker","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as a parameter, for code that is handed its tracker (a SwiftUI view given it with ","type":"text"},{"code":"tracker(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"UIKit view controller given it as a trait) rather than reading ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tracker.current","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A recording holds what the body returned, every record with its timestamp, source location and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"context, each event’s name, and the events of one type through "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting\/TrackerRecording\/events(of:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the product to test targets only. To check a tracking plan from a test, use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlanTesting"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import Testing","import TrackerTesting","","@Test func checkingOutTracksTheCartSize() async {","    let tracked = await withRecordingTracker { tracker in","        tracker.track(CheckoutStarted(cartSize: 3))","        return \"done\"","    }","    #expect(tracked.value == \"done\")","    #expect(tracked.names == [\"CheckoutStarted\"])","    #expect(tracked.events(of: CheckoutStarted.self).map(\\.cartSize) == [3])","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/testingwhatyoutrack","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers views, view controllers and asynchronous code.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://TrackerTesting/documentation/TrackerTesting/withRecordingTracker(_:)-26pul":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"withRecordingTracker","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Failure","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">((","kind":"text"},{"text":"Tracker","preciseIdentifier":"s:8Trackers7TrackerV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"Failure","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"Failure","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TrackerRecording","preciseIdentifier":"s:14TrackerTesting0A9RecordingV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting\/withRecordingTracker(_:)-26pul","url":"\/documentation\/trackertesting\/withrecordingtracker(_:)-26pul","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Runs "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":" with a tracker of its own, which it is given and which is bound to the current"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"task, then returns every event tracked through it, in the order tracked."}],"role":"symbol","title":"withRecordingTracker(_:)"},"doc://TrackerTesting/documentation/TrackerTesting/withRecordingTracker(_:)-8blfh":{"identifier":"doc